# --- let crawlers keep reading these during the move -------------------------
# Status 200 = serve in place, no redirect. These must stay readable so search
# engines can recrawl the old URLs and discover the 301s above. Listed BEFORE
# the catch-all, because _redirects is first-match-wins in file order.
/robots.txt   /robots.txt   200
/sitemap.xml  /sitemap.xml  200

# --- everything else ---------------------------------------------------------
# Anything with no counterpart goes to the main site's not-found page. That URL
# genuinely returns 404, so this is NOT a soft 404: a visitor gets a branded
# page instead of a dead subdomain, and a crawler still sees a 404 and drops
# the URL. Sending them to /blog/ instead WOULD be a soft 404, which is why
# the target is /not-found and not the blog index.
/*  https://roydipta.com/not-found  301
